{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794243827,"nonce":"Mnsf/QuwvRbzoGl6wrIiqLDQhQE=","title":"jno.precond.ams() fails on a periodic or Bloch-tied N1E system","message":"AMS builds its discrete gradient G and the interpolations Pi on the FULL edge space, and build() reads the full concrete operator. A periodic or Bloch tie makes the solve run on the reduced space P^H A P, so the first application fails with a bare shape error:\n\n  TypeError: dot_general requires contracting dimensions to have the same shape, got (n_full,) and (n_red,).\n\nReproduction: a 3-D N1E curl-curl - k^2 eps mass form on a box, with left/right and front/back ties u(left) - u(right), and fem.solve(linear=jno.solve.gmres(...), precond=jno.precond.ams()). The same form solves with lu().\n\nFix direction: reduce the AMS transfers with the tie. Build the Lagrange-side prolongation P_n with fem_dofmap.periodic_prolongation from the same tie masks and phases, take G_r = S_e G P_n and Pi_r = S_e Pi P_n (S_e selects the kept edge DOFs, so P_e G_r = G P_n), and assemble the auxiliaries from the reduced operator. With a Bloch phase G_r is complex, so the restriction is G_r^H. Until then the mismatch should raise a clear error naming the tie.","files":null}]}